{title=Leading composite approximation with a boundary layer at the right endpoint}
{description=Original sketches for $\epsilon=0.04$ and $0.08$. The dashed curve is the <outer solution> $e^{x-1}$; the inset plots the leading <inner expansion> $e(1-e^{-2X})$ against $X=(2-x)/\epsilon$.}
